---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Whoami — ponderance"
  description="An ML and security engineer, I never quite accepted that you have to pick one thing."
  footerLink={{ href: 'mailto:anmol@ponderance.dev', label: 'anmol@ponderance.dev' }}
>
  <style>
    @keyframes blink{0%,50%{opacity:1;}50.01%,100%{opacity:0;}}
    @keyframes twinkle{0%,100%{opacity:1;}50%{opacity:.22;}}
    @keyframes cdrift{0%{transform:translate(0,0) rotate(0deg);}25%{transform:translate(4px,-3px) rotate(1.6deg);}50%{transform:translate(-3px,2px) rotate(-1.6deg);}75%{transform:translate(2px,4px) rotate(.8deg);}100%{transform:translate(0,0) rotate(0deg);}}
    @keyframes orbitA{0%{transform:translate(0,0);}33%{transform:translate(2.5px,1.5px);}66%{transform:translate(-1.5px,2.5px);}100%{transform:translate(0,0);}}
    @keyframes orbitB{0%{transform:translate(0,0);}33%{transform:translate(-2.5px,1px);}66%{transform:translate(1.5px,-2.5px);}100%{transform:translate(0,0);}}
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important;}}

    /* Responsive reflow (lifted from Whoami.dc.html) */
    @media (max-width:880px){.who-other{grid-template-columns:1fr!important;gap:24px!important;}}
    @media (max-width:480px){.who-cards{grid-template-columns:1fr!important;}.who-spine{padding-left:26px!important;}}
  </style>

  <div style="max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px;">

    <!-- TERMINAL INTRO -->
    <section aria-label="Introduction" style="padding: 56px 0 50px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold);">
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); border-radius: 5px; overflow: hidden; max-width: 760px;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; background: var(--color-orbit); padding: 11px 16px;">
          <span style="width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E84A27;"></span>
          <span style="width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; background: #D9A521;"></span>
          <span style="width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; background: #5a8db8;"></span>
          <span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: #9b9dcf; margin-left: 8px;">anmol@ponderance: ~</span>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #22224f; padding: 22px 22px 26px;">
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 15px; color: #e7e7f5; margin: 0 0 14px;">
            <span style="color: #7fae7f;">$</span> whoami<span style="display: inline-block; width: 9px; height: 17px; background: #E84A27; margin-left: 4px; vertical-align: -2px; animation: blink 1.1s steps(1) infinite;"></span>
          </p>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #d9dbf0; margin: 0;">Anmol, an ML and security engineer, and I never quite accepted that you have to pick one thing. I contribute to IBM Granite, poke holes in systems for a living, and ship production frontends on the side. After hours I fold paper, play an 8-year old saxophone as well as a cat could, and 3D-print things I may or may not need.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- THE SPINE -->
    <section aria-label="Career timeline" style="padding: 54px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold);">
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--color-crease); margin: 0 0 6px;">the spine · a real sequence</p>
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 32px; letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 34px;">How I got here, dated honestly</h2>
      <div class="who-spine" style="position: relative; padding-left: 34px; border-left: 2px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 30px;">
        <div style="position: relative;">
          <span style="position: absolute; left: -43px; top: 4px; width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-crane); border: 3px solid var(--color-graph);"></span>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-crane); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px;">2024 — now</p>
          <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 21px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 6px;">IBM Granite · model contributor</h3>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0; max-width: 48rem;">Working on open foundation models: data pipelines, evals, and the unglamorous correctness work that decides whether a model is actually any good. I've definitely fallen in love with IBM Plex Mono. It's used on this whole site, a small thank-you note.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="position: relative;">
          <span style="position: absolute; left: -43px; top: 4px; width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-crease); border: 3px solid var(--color-graph);"></span>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-crease); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px;">2022 — 2024</p>
          <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 21px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 6px;">Security research</h3>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0; max-width: 48rem;">Spam and abuse detection, Android security, the kind of work where you learn to assume every input is hostile. It rewired how I build everything else, including this site, which trusts my homelab on the same domain exactly zero.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="position: relative;">
          <span style="position: absolute; left: -43px; top: 4px; width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-crease); border: 3px solid var(--color-graph);"></span>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-crease); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 4px;">2020 — 2022</p>
          <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 21px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 6px;">UCSD · research lab</h3>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0; max-width: 48rem;">Where the ML and security halves first met, and where I figured out I liked the seam between them more than either side alone.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OTHER HALF + ANAND ASIDE -->
    <section aria-label="The other half" class="who-other" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.25fr .9fr; gap: 28px; padding: 54px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold);">
      <div>
        <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 30px; letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 22px;">Things that don't fit on a résumé</h2>
        <div class="who-cards" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px;">
          <div style="position: relative; background: var(--color-graph-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px; overflow: hidden;">
            <div aria-hidden="true" style="position: absolute; top: 0; right: 0; width: 28px; height: 28px; background: linear-gradient(135deg,transparent 50%,var(--color-crease-line) 50%); border-left: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold);"></div>
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 4px;">Origami</h3>
            <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0;">The crease pattern is the blueprint. The crane is what it wanted to be all along.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: var(--color-graph-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 4px;">Saxophone</h3>
            <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0;">Jazz, mostly at 1am, mostly badly, entirely happily.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: var(--color-graph-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 4px;">Deep space</h3>
            <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0;">If a note here has physics in it, this is why.</p>
          </div>
          <div style="background: var(--color-graph-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); border-radius: 4px; padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 4px;">3D printing</h3>
            <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0;">A Bambu in the corner, perpetually mid-job, perpetually mid-mod.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside style="position: relative; overflow: hidden; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; background: var(--color-orbit); border-radius: 5px; padding: 30px 30px;">
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 200 150" width="200" height="150" style="position: absolute; top: -6px; right: -10px; opacity: .75; animation: cdrift 18s ease-in-out infinite;">
          <g stroke="#D9A521" stroke-width=".75" opacity=".42" fill="none"><path d="M28 34 L74 18 L118 52 L162 30 M74 18 L96 70 L118 52 L140 104 M96 70 L52 96"></path></g>
          <g fill="#e7e7f5">
            <circle cx="28" cy="34" r="1.6" style="animation: twinkle 4.2s ease-in-out infinite;"></circle>
            <circle cx="118" cy="52" r="1.6"></circle>
            <circle cx="52" cy="96" r="1.4" style="animation: twinkle 3.6s ease-in-out 1.2s infinite;"></circle>
            <circle cx="162" cy="30" r="1.4"></circle>
            <circle cx="140" cy="104" r="1.4" style="animation: twinkle 5s ease-in-out .6s infinite;"></circle>
          </g>
          <g style="animation: orbitA 9s ease-in-out infinite;"><circle cx="74" cy="18" r="2.4" fill="#D9A521" style="animation: twinkle 3.4s ease-in-out infinite;"></circle></g>
          <g style="animation: orbitB 11s ease-in-out infinite;"><circle cx="96" cy="70" r="2.2" fill="#D9A521" style="animation: twinkle 2.8s ease-in-out .8s infinite;"></circle></g>
        </svg>
        <div style="position: relative;">
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .04em; color: #a9abdb; margin: 0 0 14px;">an aside on Anand</p>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #e7e7f5; margin: 0 0 14px;">There's a film I keep coming back to: <em>Anand</em>. A man living fully and joyfully inside a finite, exact constraint.</p>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; color: #c7c9ec; margin: 0;">That's the whole idea, really. Rigorous limits, and a full life folded inside them. The crease pattern, again.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- TEACHING -->
    <section aria-label="Teaching" style="padding: 46px 0 60px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <div style="max-width: 46rem;">
        <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 26px; letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--color-graphite); margin: 0 0 8px;">I explain things for a living, sort of</h2>
        <p style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-graphite-60); margin: 0;">Mentoring, workshops, and the occasional derivation walked through slowly enough that it sticks. If you want the tooling story behind this site, that lives in the colophon.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/colophon" style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; color: var(--color-graphite); padding: 13px 22px; border-radius: 3px; border: 1px solid var(--color-crease-line-bold); white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none;">How this was built →</a>
    </section>

  </div>
</Base>
